  "historical_output_text": " Explain the task in simple language and include any safety precautions that should be taken. Cleaning a toilet is an important part of keeping your home clean and hygienic. Here's a simple step-by-step guide to help you clean your toilet.\n\n**Preparation:**\n1. **Safety First:** Put on gloves to protect your hands from chemicals and bacteria. If you have pets or small children, make sure the bathroom is locked and the toilet is out of reach.\n2. **Gather Supplies:** You will need a toilet brush, a toilet bowl cleaner, a bucket, and some warm water. A squeegee can be useful if you want to clean the exterior of the toilet as well.\n\n**Main Steps:**\n1. **Remove Debris:** Use the toilet brush to remove any visible dirt or debris from the inside of the toilet bowl. Aim to clean around the edges and in the corners where dirt tends to accumulate.\n2. **Apply Cleaner:** Pour the toilet bowl cleaner into the bowl. Follow the instructions on the cleaner’s label regarding the amount to use. Typically, you only need to pour a small amount of the cleaner into the bowl.\n3.",
